                <pb facs="0718" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.01/192: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-27T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 28—12:24
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>66. Your 52 April 24, 4 p.m. The powers in the Supreme Council have recognized
                    Albania <hi rendition="#italic">de jure</hi>. Of these powers England and Italy
                    have sent Ministers. France is represented only by a consul at Scutari. Japan
                    has no representative. The other countries which have accorded <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de jure</hi> recognition are Finland, Switzerland,
                    Belgium and Jugoslavia and of these only Jugoslavia is represented, having a
                    Chargé d’Affaires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
